============================================================
15. CORE RULES
============================================================

RULE 1

A seed germinates once.


RULE 2

Seed-coat splitting is a germination event,
not reproductive multiplication.


RULE 3

After establishment, repeated "splitting" is represented
as vegetative modular growth.


RULE 4

Modular growth is bounded by carrying capacity.


RULE 5

Environmental quality multiplies modular growth through Omega.


RULE 6

Nitrate has a bounded response rather than providing
unlimited growth.


RULE 7

Nitrate is NOT used as a male/female/intersex switch.


RULE 8

Hermaphroditic/intersex reproductive expression remains
separate from germination.


RULE 9

Vegetative modules are NOT called seeds.


RULE 10

A new true seed enters the system only through the
reproductive pathway.


